WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.450
Wow, where to begin?

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:13.090
Alright, in case you missed it, I was off
the grid for an entire month, and I have the

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:19.180
facial hair to prove it...my beard even has
a Twitter account already, yes really.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.450
Over the past 30 days, I've had no phone,
no email, no Twitter and no digital noise

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.910
in my life.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:30.890
I also didn't watch any news or have one single
conversation about politics the entire time

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.550
I was gone.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.449
What I did do during this time was a combination
of writing my book, relaxing, some gardening,

00:00:37.449 --> 00:00:41.440
taking long walks with my dog and spending
time with friends and family.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.539
As I said in our livestream yesterday, I'm
incredibly grateful and humbled by those of

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:51.449
you who support The Rubin Report on Patreon
and PayPal for letting me and my crew carve

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:56.800
out this precious bit of time to rest, rejuvenate
and come back more focused than ever.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.300
I learned a few life lessons in this last
month, including writing a book is far more

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.670
intense and introspective than you can possibly
imagine...

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:08.550
so just give me a little more time to work
on it.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:12.480
Unsurprisingly, the news cycle kept on spinning
without me, and I'm just now catching up on

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.610
everything I missed.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:18.750
From the terror attack in Barcelona, to the
events in Charleston to devastation of Hurricane

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:24.750
Harvey and now Trumps reversal of DACA, there's
no shortage of news for me to catch up on.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:29.990
For this Direct Message though, I want to
look forward not backwards, and instead share

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:33.680
some thoughts on the future of what we're
going to be doing around here.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.970
I consider today to be the first episode of
season 3 of The Rubin Report.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.980
Our first season of The Rubin Report as an
interview show began two years ago when we

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:47.270
launched on Ora TV with my interview with
Sam Harris.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:51.610
Over the next year the show began to blow
up as we focused more and more on free speech

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:55.890
and the battle for logic and reason to be
put back into public discourse.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:01.180
About a year ago, we left Ora and went fully
independent so we could 100% control the content

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.940
we were creating as well as the business behind
it -- I consider this phase of our show to

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.320
be Season 2.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:12.750
I don't know if any show out there has a more
diverse guest list over the past two years

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:19.209
and I intended on expanding on it, going deeper
on the important issues more than ever before.

00:02:19.209 --> 00:02:24.379
Your support allows me to do what I think
is right, instead of focusing on what content

00:02:24.379 --> 00:02:25.709
will make a dime.

00:02:25.709 --> 00:02:31.700
Whether YouTube demonetizes us, or the algorithms
work against us because of the dangerous "controversial"

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:37.129
topics we cover, The Rubin Report will continue
to cover the issues that really matter, having

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:41.370
the detailed, nuanced conversations you'll
never get on mainstream news.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:44.959
With this in mind, I'm thrilled to be launching
season 3 of The Rubin Report with one of the

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:50.110
few people I find consistently making some
sense of the endless noise that we are constantly

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.290
bombarded with.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:56.840
Phil Defranco, host of the aptly titled Philip
Defranco Show is one of the guys I turn to

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:01.200
to get unbiased, sourced, and credible analysis
of current events.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.480
As one of the first big YouTubers around he's
had an interesting personal and political

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.980
evolution himself, something he's done in
front of the camera for years now.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.999
Our friends at Learn Liberty are partnering
with us for this episode and Phil has requested

00:03:13.999 --> 00:03:20.170
that his honorarium for this show be given
to the Polycystic Disease Foundation, a cause

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.810
which is very personal to him.

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:26.029
After the show Learn Liberty will be writing
a check of $1,500 dollars to the foundation

00:03:26.029 --> 00:03:31.489
-- you can find out more about this cause
at PKD cure dot org.

00:03:31.489 --> 00:03:37.180
Alright, I'm back, bearded and ready to talk
about the important issues of the day.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:41.169
If there's a specific issue you want us to
cover or a special person you want us to talk

00:03:41.169 --> 00:03:44.730
to this season let us know in the comments
right down below.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.030
Since I've been off the Internet for awhile
I assume all YouTube comments are positive

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:50.421
and friendly now, so I look forward to seeing
what you come up with...

